      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Row 76. Pets unknown: no fetched page covers Pittosporum tenuifolium; the ASPCA page fetched (https://www.aspca.org/pet-care/aspca-poison-control/toxic-and-non-toxic-plants/japanese-pittosporum) is for P. tobira, a different species, and lists it non-toxic to dogs, cats and horses; that is not carried over. No NC State Plant Toolbox page for this species turned up in the search. Care comes from the RHS species profile (moist but well-drained or well-drained, full sun or partial shade, H4 = -10 to -5 C, 4 to 8 m by 2.5 to 4 m, 10 to 20 years to maturity, bushy, evergreen) and the RHS genus growing guide: well-drained soil, water for the first couple of years in dry spells (large specimens up to five), fairly drought tolerant once established, may still need water on quick-draining soil or in a hot spot, containers only for the smaller cultivars, leaf drop from waterlogging or long dry spells, mulch 5 to 7.5 cm. The guide is about the genus, so everything taken from it is from_knowledge_verify. Growth rate: neither page gives one. let_top_dry and 7 days are the agent's mapping and a guess. Es and it names are machine drafts."
      },
